Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:08.48,Default,,0,0,800,,{\b1\4c&H0000FF&\fs40}LAUGHING MAN FANSUBS{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.79,0:00:09.29,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I'm a soldier - that means I'm
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.49,0:00:12.69,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Both a defendant and the judge
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.49,0:00:18.09,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I am standing on both ends of the flame
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.77,0:00:23.22,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Rounding curves
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.52,0:00:26.12,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Overtaking life and death,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.62,0:00:31.97,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I run and fight with false shadows
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.27,0:00:38.27,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,No matter how many threads of\Ndeception are woven together,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.67,0:00:46.17,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,The truth shall illuminate\Nthe face of light
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.17,0:00:49.97,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your tears for the day
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.27,0:00:53.27,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,When our pain is far behind
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.67,0:00:56.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,On your feet, come with me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.57,0:00:59.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We are soldiers stand or die
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.07,0:01:02.97,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your fears, take your place
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.17,0:01:06.17,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save them for the judgement day
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.47,0:01:09.37,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Fast and free, follow me
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.67,0:01:14.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Time to make the sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.87,0:01:20.47,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We rise or fall
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.38,0:02:00.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The refugees are now completely isolated.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.28,0:02:08.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All that remains is for me to observe how these\Npeople, who are so intolerant of solitude,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.75,0:02:11.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,will achieve the conclusion I have imagined...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.99,0:02:28.44,Sign - Copy,,575,0,500,,{\b1\i0}Dejima, Airstrike{\b0\i1}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.03,0:02:33.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They won't be backing down if they only\Nreturned fire after one of their own was shot.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.13,0:02:39.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We have a report from Strategic Intelligence\Nthat all the remaining plutonium is in Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.33,0:02:41.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We should be ordering the mechanised\Ntroops to advance and end this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.93,0:02:45.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,instead of waiting for the\Ninspection team to arrive.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.33,0:02:48.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, we have other information
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.23,0:02:50.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,indicating that if we send\Ntroops into Dejima, the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.51,0:02:53.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,refugees will commit suicide\Nby detonating a nuclear bomb.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.13,0:02:58.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We can afford to wait to deploy the troops until\Nafter we hit the refugee forces major strongholds.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.43,0:03:02.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Why don't we deploy those unmanned choppers?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.67,0:03:19.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Prime Minister Kayabuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.87,0:03:24.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You are relieved of your post as Prime Minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.17,0:03:27.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is the meaning of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.67,0:03:28.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And the reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.67,0:03:31.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Your request for a UN inspection team,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.77,0:03:36.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,based solely on your personal judgement, could be\Nconstrued as an act of treason during a time of crisis.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.77,0:03:42.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You will be kept in protective custody\Nuntil this situation is resolved.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.27,0:03:42.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Chief.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.07,0:03:45.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Who... on what authority...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.77,0:03:47.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.77,0:03:49.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Chief Aramaki of Section 9.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.77,0:03:54.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You and your men are also\Nsuspected of abetting treason.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.97,0:03:56.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Please return to the office.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.97,0:03:58.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey! What are you guys...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.46,0:04:14.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We have been unable to make contact\Nwith Chief Aramaki for six hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.76,0:04:16.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is he still underground in\Nthe Prime Minister's office?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.06,0:04:17.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.56,0:04:19.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.26,0:04:22.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then please tell him this\Nwhen you get through to him:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.36,0:04:26.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's probably the result of information\Nmanipulation by the Cabinet Intelligence Agency,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.86,0:04:31.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but there's a rumour circulating that the\Nrefugees will detonate the plutonium.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.36,0:04:33.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There must be something else to that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.60,0:04:34.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.26,0:04:44.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Knowing you, though,\NI'm sure you've already uncovered something.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.87,0:05:03.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's the same as the other time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.57,0:05:06.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The government intended to do\Nthis from the very beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.07,0:05:08.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Damn SDF bastards!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.57,0:05:11.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Just try coming into Dejima!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.17,0:05:12.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Put down your weapons!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.07,0:05:14.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Put them away right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.77,0:05:15.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.57,0:05:16.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.97,0:05:18.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.57,0:05:21.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If you keep your weapons out of\Nsight, they won't attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.27,0:05:26.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He is Comrade Kuze?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.83,0:05:51.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They're coming!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.03,0:06:17.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's out of control.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.03,0:06:18.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.73,0:06:21.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Get some good men together.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.93,0:06:25.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I will reconnect everyone to my cyberbrain!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.33,0:06:26.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.19,0:06:34.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's the exact same thing as the joint exercise that was\Nconducted in the Niihama Refugee Residential Sector.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.09,0:06:39.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Once we enter Dejima airspace, our military\NID code will probably become invalid.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.49,0:06:44.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Jigabachi will indiscriminately\Nattack any mechanised unit
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.39,0:06:46.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that differ in appearance from themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.69,0:06:48.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It can't be helped.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.29,0:06:49.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Bomer, hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.79,0:06:50.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.29,0:06:56.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right, Bomer. Switch with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.69,0:07:09.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The attack's begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.09,0:07:11.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.29,0:07:13.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But it doesn't seem like we'll see any action.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.69,0:07:16.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There won't be a ground assault\Nunless the plutonium is retrieved.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.09,0:07:18.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then what's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.39,0:07:21.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That has nothing to do with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.69,0:07:24.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,GSDF Special Ops are secretly entering Dejima
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.59,0:07:26.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to retrieve the nuke.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.33,0:07:37.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.13,0:07:39.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll enter the jamming zone soon!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.33,0:07:42.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Even after the comm link is cut\Noff, leave it open.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.83,0:07:45.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Keep tabs on any marine activity, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.43,0:07:46.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.63,0:07:50.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Jigabachi units are currently\Ncircling at regular intervals.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.73,0:07:55.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We believe that coming in within that tall structure's\Nshadow, at low altitude, would be best...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.73,0:07:57.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The comm link's gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.93,0:07:59.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.86,0:08:08.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A unit with a different ID code is\Napproaching Dejima from the north.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.16,0:08:11.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's disappeared into the ECM area.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.17,0:08:15.76,Default,,0,0,850,,{\fs35}{\b1\i1}ECM or Electronic Countermeasures refers \N to any technique inhibiting the enemy's ability \N to make use of the electromagnetic spectrum{\b0\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.46,0:08:12.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.96,0:08:14.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Follow the same course.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.76,0:08:15.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.85,0:08:27.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The comm link is finally gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.15,0:08:31.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, I hope Batou-san's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.65,0:08:36.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Those gloomy AIs were pretty vicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.35,0:08:36.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, true.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.15,0:08:37.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm worried.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.85,0:08:38.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.35,0:08:38.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It was really scary.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.25,0:08:41.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh yeah, I wonder if he was able\Nto catch up with Ishikawa-San.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.75,0:08:42.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.42,0:08:46.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, were you able to meet up with Ishikawa-San?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.42,0:08:49.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,As if I could get there that quickly!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.42,0:08:52.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm in physical transit on the ground!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.12,0:08:53.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right. Sorry, sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.72,0:08:55.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What about you, Ishikawa-San?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.42,0:08:57.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm also on my way.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.12,0:09:01.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I can't hurry too much, or I'll get caught.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.42,0:09:08.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How's the Major doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.12,0:09:11.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We still have her on visual feed,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.12,0:09:12.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,so we know she's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.72,0:09:13.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.92,0:09:17.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But since the Jigabachi have command of the air,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.32,0:09:19.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the situation is very dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.12,0:09:21.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We can't get in touch with the Chief, either...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.62,0:09:26.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems we have no choice\Nbut to make our own decisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.02,0:09:29.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The refugees and Kuze;
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.42,0:09:31.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the government and Gouda;
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.12,0:09:33.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the Chief and the Major; and ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.02,0:09:40.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems the one who has the best standalone\Nstrategy will determine the outcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.03,0:09:46.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.13,0:09:48.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Section 4's chopper has entered Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.93,0:09:49.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.93,0:09:54.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It looks like we'll be able\Nto retrieve the plutonium.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.73,0:10:00.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Retrieving the plutonium wasn't the\Nreal reason we deployed Section 4.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.13,0:10:02.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Sir, by that you mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.93,0:10:04.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You'll soon understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.74,0:10:26.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's no good. We can't land.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.94,0:10:28.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There's rubble everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.44,0:10:29.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We don't have any choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.64,0:10:31.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll rappel down one by one.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.44,0:10:39.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Ready, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.76,0:10:48.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.33,0:10:57.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.64,0:11:10.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The rudder's been hit!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.88,0:11:53.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How is it going, Proto?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.98,0:11:55.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Can we reach the Tachikomas?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.68,0:11:57.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes, somehow.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.28,0:11:58.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.18,0:11:58.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.68,0:12:02.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I wouldn't have been able to\Ndo this if I'd been by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.38,0:12:03.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.38,0:12:07.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You're able to act as the situation demands.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.18,0:12:11.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I wonder if Prime Minister Kayabuki is all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.88,0:12:14.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,She is being held captive somewhere
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.08,0:12:20.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,since they will want to keep the coup from the\Nmedia until after this situation is resolved.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.78,0:12:23.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In order to shift responsibility\Nto her after the fact...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.88,0:12:24.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.08,0:12:27.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, until there is a public announcement,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.48,0:12:30.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,she still retains her powers as a Prime Minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.58,0:12:33.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There will be situations in which\Nher authority will prove invaluable.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.78,0:12:35.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.58,0:12:38.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Senpai, I was able to contact the Tachikomas.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.38,0:12:43.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems the Major and the others have\Nentered Dejima with the plutonium.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.58,0:12:44.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Dejima?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.98,0:12:47.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see. They've thought things through.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.38,0:12:48.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So, what is the situation?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.78,0:12:50.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's not good.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.28,0:12:53.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems there was a scuffle\Nbetween the refugees and the SDF,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.28,0:12:57.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and the SDF assault choppers ran an air\Nraid on Dejima's military strongholds.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.38,0:13:01.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The chopper our people were in\Nwas also attacked a while ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.38,0:13:01.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.08,0:13:04.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then, the Major and the old man...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.38,0:13:09.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Since there are ECM covering Dejima,\Nthey have not been able to contact the team
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.18,0:13:11.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to confirm their survival.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.88,0:13:18.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Have the Tachikomas continue to keep us informed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.68,0:13:19.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.82,0:13:27.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Bastard...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.93,0:13:54.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Batou. I'll go on ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.93,0:13:59.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Where are you, Kuze?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.34,0:14:40.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.24,0:14:43.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We still have time before\Nthe patrol aircraft comes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.33,0:15:01.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Shit.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.93,0:15:05.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This is bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.03,0:15:08.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll be surrounded by refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.69,0:15:18.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The target is still nearby.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.99,0:15:19.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Get moving!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.09,0:15:21.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.39,0:15:24.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They followed us in?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.19,0:15:27.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We can't use our comm systems.\NDon't use thermo-optical camouflage;
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.69,0:15:30.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,we'll risk friendly fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.77,0:15:34.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Which unit are they from?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.77,0:15:36.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're in deep shit.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.67,0:15:39.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's a GSDF special forces team.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.75,0:15:48.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We don't see Batou-San and the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.45,0:15:51.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A different chopper came to the crash\Nsite -- I wonder what that's about.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.65,0:15:54.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It looks like some soldiers\Noffloaded, but it's hard to tell.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.75,0:15:56.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I can't find the Major, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.65,0:15:58.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Maybe they're using thermo-optical camouflage.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.05,0:16:01.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, hey, what's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.85,0:16:07.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Aegis ships and chopper carriers that surround\NDejima began pulling back a short while ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.15,0:16:12.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The minesweepers are\Ndeploying micro machines, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.32,0:16:14.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let's see...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.16,0:16:19.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You're right...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.76,0:16:21.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In the event of a nuclear explosion,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.86,0:16:23.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,you can't minimise the effects of radiation
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.06,0:16:27.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,if you don't deploy the micro\Nmachines in advance, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.66,0:16:30.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's the strategy where you suck the\Nmicro machines into the affected area
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.36,0:16:32.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by taking advantage of the backdraft\Nafter the nuclear bomb detonates.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.06,0:16:35.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I still don't understand this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.86,0:16:39.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Maybe it's insurance,\Nin case the refugees use the nukes?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.36,0:16:40.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No way.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.36,0:16:44.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's understandable if the SDF believes\Nthere are nuclear weapons on the island,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.76,0:16:46.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but according to the Major's analysis,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.56,0:16:51.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,at least the Chief Cabinet Secretary\Nand Gouda know there are none, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.66,0:16:55.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Maybe it's another act, for heightened realism?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.56,0:16:57.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's possible,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.46,0:16:59.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but even so, it's still a little too realistic.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.86,0:17:02.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How would you analyse the situation, Proto-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.26,0:17:02.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.46,0:17:04.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let me see...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.06,0:17:06.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.76,0:17:08.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What do you think this is?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.26,0:17:09.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What, what?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.56,0:17:09.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.56,0:17:10.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What, what?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.86,0:17:13.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Three hundred seventy kilometres\Neast of the Okinawa Atoll,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.16,0:17:16.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,an enormous lump of iron is surfacing
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.56,0:17:20.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,just within Japan's exclusive economic zone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.36,0:17:23.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Could this be...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.06,0:17:27.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,one of the American Empire's nuclear submarines?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.56,0:17:29.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,One of the Empire's nuclear submarines?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.10,0:17:35.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I wonder what meaning is behind\Nits presence within our EEZ
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.40,0:17:40.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It would mean the sub appeared due to\Nsome action on the part of the government.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.90,0:17:45.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Do you mean they'd actually fire\Na nuclear missile at Dejima?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.30,0:17:49.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The circumstances seem to indicate\Nthat this would be the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.40,0:17:52.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Gouda was controlling everything,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.90,0:17:55.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,knowing this would happen\Nfrom the very beginning...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.50,0:17:59.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and the Chief Cabinet Secretary was accelerating\Nthe Security Pact for the same reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.80,0:18:00.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Impossible...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.00,0:18:02.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's not unreasonable.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.80,0:18:05.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The final acts in Gouda's scenario\Nwould probably go along the lines of
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.00,0:18:12.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the refugees attempting suicide with a nuclear\Nbomb after being surrounded by the SDF.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.30,0:18:14.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Both the funds generated by\NPoseidon's bribery and the public
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.93,0:18:17.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,funds that disappeared from\Nthe Ministry of Foreign Affairs
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.50,0:18:22.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,must have been used to make the\NAmerican Empire fire the nuclear missile
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.40,0:18:29.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by those who intend to reset everything in secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.70,0:18:34.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And now, the plutonium has actually\Nbeen taken into Dejima by Section 9...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.60,0:18:37.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Chief, let's bring back Prime Minister Kayabuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.60,0:18:39.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,As you said earlier,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.20,0:18:42.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,she is still the Prime Minister of\NJapan from a diplomatic standpoint.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.10,0:18:47.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Her authority may still be able\Nto prevent the nuclear attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.13,0:18:49.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.73,0:18:57.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They never thought to search me,\Neven though you and Proto were.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.31,0:19:05.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Proto, do you know where the\NPrime Minister is being held?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.81,0:19:07.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Okay, I'll run a search now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.72,0:19:19.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Proto!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.02,0:19:21.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.02,0:19:24.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Damn, an offensive firewall...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.41,0:19:38.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Sen... pai...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.31,0:19:40.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Proto.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.41,0:19:45.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Prime Minister's... room...\NI got... the location...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.31,0:19:49.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Proto, you were an android?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.91,0:19:51.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.11,0:19:52.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I am...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.51,0:19:54.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,a prototype...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.31,0:19:57.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,bioroid...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.32,0:20:10.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They're here!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.02,0:20:12.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.31,0:20:16.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't panic.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.61,0:20:18.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This is an infrared-guided missile.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.91,0:20:20.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You can hit the target with your eyes shut.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.51,0:20:23.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They won't be expecting any stingers.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.01,0:20:25.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There they are.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.61,0:20:30.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.46,0:21:02.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Got 'em!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.26,0:21:04.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Enemy choppers will come this way at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.06,0:21:06.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let's get out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.17,0:21:16.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.42,0:21:24.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,At this rate, we wouldn't be\Nable to make any moves, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.72,0:21:26.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You guys go out first.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.32,0:21:28.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll go last and bring the plutonium.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.02,0:21:31.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll meet in the building behind us.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.12,0:21:32.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's a maze inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.62,0:21:34.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We can still win!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.27,0:21:42.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They're coming. Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.47,0:21:44.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Two-man teams, in two sets.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.27,0:21:45.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.64,0:22:15.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They're using thermo-optical camouflage!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.74,0:22:18.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems our targets aren't regular grunts.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.64,0:22:20.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.54,0:22:26.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,According to our orders, the ones who took the\Nplutonium were five low-ranking soldiers...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.34,0:22:28.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right, split into two groups.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.84,0:22:31.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll pursue them in formation B!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.14,0:22:32.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.66,0:23:10.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Finding out a galaxy
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.01,0:23:14.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of planets and stars within me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.11,0:23:17.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Listening to each of them
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.86,0:23:21.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,singing the same silent melody.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.66,0:23:25.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I've never seen such beauty
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.81,0:23:28.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in possibility...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.06,0:23:32.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No smack of doubt or fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.26,0:23:35.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.16,0:23:36.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I hear a voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.69,0:23:39.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(And show the light)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.75,0:23:39.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,hear a voice calling out to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.97,0:23:41.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.63,0:23:43.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see inside
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.23,0:23:46.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(the time is right)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.26,0:23:47.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,see the light now ever holding me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.66,0:23:48.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.21,0:23:51.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All I need,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.20,0:23:49.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(All the truth)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.08,0:23:54.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to make all this reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.60,0:23:55.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(it's inside)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.90,0:23:57.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The beauty within the shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.57,0:23:58.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(deep within the shell)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.99,0:23:59.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(within the shell)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.97,0:24:01.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.90,0:24:04.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I hear a voice
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.97,0:24:06.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(And show the light)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.20,0:24:08.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,hear a voice calling out to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.56,0:24:07.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.53,0:24:12.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(the time is now)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.75,0:24:10.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see inside,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.95,0:24:14.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,see the light now ever holding me.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.07,0:24:15.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.37,0:24:16.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(All the truth)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.80,0:24:17.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,all I need,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.85,0:24:19.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to make all this reality,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.92,0:24:22.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it's inside
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.77,0:24:25.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,right here within the shell.
